# One pair per workspace you configure in ~/.slack-mcp/workspaces.json.
# The user token (xoxp-...) is copied from the app's OAuth & Permissions page
# after installing it into that workspace.
SLACK_TOKEN_NEXTDOORDEV=xoxp-...
SLACK_TOKEN_PLAYFIELD=xoxp-...

# Only needed if you're running the optional Socket Mode daemon
# (daemon/socket-listener.ts). Generated from the app's Socket Mode settings
# page. Each workspace entry used by the daemon needs an `appTokenEnv` field
# in workspaces.json pointing at the matching variable below, in addition to
# its existing `tokenEnv`. See daemon/README.md before enabling — an
# unattended busy channel wired to trigger an agent per message can burn
# through model quota quickly.
SLACK_APPTOKEN_NEXTDOORDEV=xapp-...
SLACK_APPTOKEN_PLAYFIELD=xapp-...
